{
	"name": "Calcite Gecko",
	"type": "object",
	"img": "icons/creatures/reptiles/lizard-iguana-green.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>The skin of these small lizards resembles the calcite stone for which they are named, And they can sometimes be spotted when they glint in the sun. Typically found in mountainous regions and in and around caves, calcite geckos are drawn to deposits of precious and semiprecious gemstones and minerals. Shy by nature, they usually flee when seen. Adventurers who succeed on a Survival check to track a fleeing calcite gecko will be led to a mineable deposit of raw gems. Refer to the following table for the DC and resulting amount of gems found:</p><table><thead><tr><th style=\"text-align: left;\"><p>DC</p></th><th style=\"text-align: center;\"><p>Result</p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"text-align: left;\"><p>10</p></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><p>[[/r 1d4 + 2]] gp raw gems</p></td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align: left;\"><p>14</p></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><p>[[/r 2d4 + 2]] gp raw gems</p></td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align: left;\"><p>18</p></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><p>[[/r 4d4 + 4]] gp raw gems</p></td></tr></tbody></table>",
